      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:2:1:111:5",
      "text": [
        " كَانَ أَمِيرُ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ ( عليه السلام ) يَقُولُ لَا تُبْدِيَنَّ عَنْ وَاضِحَةٍ وَ قَدْ عَمِلْتَ الْأَعْمَالَ الْفَاضِحَةَ وَ لَا يَأْمَنِ الْبَيَاتَ مَنْ عَمِلَ السَّيِّئَاتِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali, from his father, from Al Nowfaly, from Al Sakuny, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘Amir Al-<span class=\"iTxt\">Momin</span>een<sup>asws</sup> was saying: ‘You should not show (your teeth) clearly and you have done the shameful deed, nor should he sleep securely, the one who committed the sins’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "5. Ali has narrated from his father from al-Nawfali from al-Sakuni from abu ‘Abd Allah (a.s.) who has said the following: “Amir al-Mu’minin, Ali ibn abu Talib (a.s.) has said, ‘You must never show your teeth (smile) when you have committed disgraceful deeds and never feel safe from misfortune to strike you due to (your) sinful deeds.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
